Chapter: RocMatchColorRank
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_match_tests.zig, "match-dt:
 four-tag nominal union dispatches every arm":

     Color := [Red, Green, Blue, Yellow]
     rank : Color -> I64
     rank = |c| match c { Red => 1, Green => 2, Blue => 3, Yellow => 4 }
     main = List.map([Red, Green, Blue, Yellow], rank)      [1, 2, 3, 4]

 The map is a comprehension; the list prints joined with commas.

Section: Types

  Color =
   | Red
   | Green
   | Blue
   | Yellow

Section: Functions

  rank : Color -> Integer
  rank (c) =
   when c
    is Red -> 1
    is Green -> 2
    is Blue -> 3
    is Yellow -> 4

  join-ints : List Integer, Integer -> Text
  join-ints (xs) (i) =
   if i >= list-length xs then ""
   else if i + 1 == list-length xs then show (list-at xs i)
   else show (list-at xs i) & ", " & join-ints xs (i + 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   let colors = [Red, Green, Blue, Yellow]
   in let ranks = for c in colors -> rank c
   in print-line-uni ("[" & join-ints ranks 0 & "]")
  end
